Creating a full-fledged Tetris game in PHP is a bit involved, but I can give you a basic script to get you started. This will be a simplified version that uses a text-based interface to display the game.

**tetris.php**
```php
<?php

// Define the Tetris grid size
$gridSize = 10;

// Define the Tetris piece shapes
$pieces = array(
    "I" => array(array(1, 1, 1, 1)),
    "J" => array(array(1, 0, 0), array(1, 1, 1)),
    "L" => array(array(0, 0, 1), array(1, 1, 1)),
    "O" => array(array(1, 1), array(1, 1)),
    "S" => array(array(0, 1, 1), array(1, 1, 0)),
    "T" => array(array(0, 1, 0), array(1, 1, 1)),
    "Z" => array(array(1, 1, 0), array(0, 1, 1))
);

// Define the game state
$grid = array_fill(0, $gridSize, array_fill(0, $gridSize, 0));
$score = 0;
$level = 1;

// Function to draw the game grid
function drawGrid($grid) {
    foreach ($grid as $row) {
        echo implode(" ", $row) . "\n";
    }
}

// Function to clear a row from the grid
function clearRow($grid, $row) {
    $grid[$row] = array_fill(0, $gridSize, 0);
    return $grid;
}

// Function to move a piece down
function moveDown($grid, $piece, $x, $y) {
    if ($y + count($piece) <= $gridSize) {
        for ($i = 0; $i < count($piece); $i++) {
            $grid[$y + $i][$x + count($piece) - 1] = 1;
        }
        return array($grid, $x, $y + 1);
    } else {
        return array($grid, $x, $y);
    }
}

// Function to move a piece left
function moveLeft($grid, $piece, $x, $y) {
    if ($x - 1 >= 0) {
        $oldPiece = array();
        foreach ($piece as $row) {
            $oldPiece[] = array_merge(array_fill(0, $x - 1, 0), $row);
        }
        if (!anyCollide($grid, $oldPiece, $x - 1, $y)) {
            for ($i = 0; $i < count($piece); $i++) {
                $grid[$y][$x + count($piece) - 1 - $i] = 1;
            }
            return array($grid, $x - 1, $y);
        }
    }
    return array($grid, $x, $y);
}

// Function to move a piece right
function moveRight($grid, $piece, $x, $y) {
    if ($x + count($piece) < $gridSize) {
        $oldPiece = array();
        foreach ($piece as $row) {
            $oldPiece[] = array_merge($row, array_fill(0, $gridSize - $x - count($piece), 0));
        }
        if (!anyCollide($grid, $oldPiece, $x, $y)) {
            for ($i = 0; $i < count($piece); $i++) {
                $grid[$y][$x + $i] = 1;
            }
            return array($grid, $x + 1, $y);
        }
    }
    return array($grid, $x, $y);
}

// Function to check for collisions
function anyCollide($grid, $piece, $x, $y) {
    foreach ($piece as $i => $row) {
        foreach ($row as $j => $cell) {
            if ($cell && $grid[$y + $i][$x + $j]) {
                return true;
            }
        }
    }
    return false;
}

// Main game loop
while (true) {
    // Draw the game grid
    drawGrid($grid);

    // Get the user's input
    $input = trim(fgets(STDIN));

    // Move the current piece
    if ($input == 'd') {
        list($grid, $x, $y) = moveDown($grid, $pieces[substr($currentPiece, 0, 1)], $x, $y);
    } elseif ($input == 'a') {
        list($grid, $x, $y) = moveLeft($grid, $pieces[substr($currentPiece, 0, 1)], $x, $y);
    } elseif ($input == 's') {
        list($grid, $x, $y) = moveRight($grid, $pieces[substr($currentPiece, 0, 1)], $x, $y);
    } elseif ($input == 'q') {
        break;
    }

    // Check if the piece has reached the bottom
    if ($y + count($pieces[substr($currentPiece, 0, 1)]) >= $gridSize) {
        // Clear the full row
        for ($i = 0; $i < $gridSize; $i++) {
            $grid[$y][$i] = 0;
        }

        // Increase the score
        $score += 100;

        // Increase the level
        $level++;
    }

    // Choose a new random piece
    $currentPiece = array_rand($pieces);

    // Pause the game for a bit
    usleep(500000);
}

// Display the final score
echo "Game over! Your final score is: $score\n";

?>
```
This script will create a Tetris game with a text-based interface. You can use the 'd' key to move the piece down, the 'a' key to move it left, the 's' key to move it right, and the 'q' key to quit the game.

Note that this is a very simplified version of Tetris, and there are many features that are not included (such as scoring, level-up, line clearing, etc.). You can add these features yourself by modifying the script.

